# Netlify / Cloudflare Pages redirects, read from the build output. Rules match top to bottom.
#
# The API never lives on this static host. A /v1 or /api request that lands here was sent to the
# wrong host, so it gets a real 404 instead of the SPA's HTML with a 200 (which a first curl would
# mistake for success). If the API is ever proxied through this origin, replace these two lines with
#   /v1/*   https://api.<domain>/v1/:splat   200
#   /api/*  https://api.<domain>/api/:splat  200
/v1/*  /404.html  404
/v1    /404.html  404
/api/*  /404.html  404
/api    /404.html  404

# Deep links such as /docs/api are client-side routes, so every other path serves index.html and
# React Router resolves it.
/*  /index.html  200
